{% set local_problem %}
<p>Lacey's Spring's hilly terrain creates drainage challenges that surface solutions can't always solve. You can't extend a downspout uphill. Natural drainage patterns on hillsides may concentrate water in problematic areas. Valley properties may have water flowing toward them from multiple directions.</p>

<p>Underground drains bypass these limitations. Buried pipes can route water to the optimal discharge point regardless of what the surface terrain looks like.</p>

<p>Rural Lacey's Spring properties often have excellent discharge options — wooded areas, natural drainage swales, or low points far from any structure. Underground drains let us take advantage of these options.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes that connect to your downspouts and carry water to a discharge point far from your home. On hilly terrain, we design systems that work with the natural grade while routing water where it needs to go.</p>
{% endset %}

